001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"F06 implementation and local validation\n\n- `docs/README.md` is the only changed project file.\n- The landing page contains distinct client, contributor, architecture, ADR, operations, research, and historical evidence routes.\n- The required CLI, MCP, adoption, contribution, and implementation paths remain discoverable.\n- All three troubleshooting cases and their remedies remain present.\n- The primary directory contains all 67 maintained top-level Markdown pages exactly once. The three required historical evidence pages each retain one primary entry.\n- The outdated six-relation and shared-ADR-number claims are absent. Generated artifact tables remain on `docs/generated-artifacts.md`.\n- `scripts/check_docs_index.py --check`, the one-off uniqueness check, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- The focused documentation suite passes all 35 tests.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass on origin/main at 960fbfef2f.\n- A supplementary full project run passed 15,577 tests with 63 skips, 297 deselections, and one expected failure before the non-overlapping fast-forward. Per operator direction, Markdown-only changes do not require another full local suite. Gerrit Verified will supply the current-patch project gate.\n- The signed plan remains certified after the fast-forward and checkbox completion.","timestamp":1787375657836838001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"F06 commit 4a71f30c462ab95f4872165a98ca57e6265fd854 passed the canonical ticket trailer verifier and was pushed to Gerrit change 2068. Patch set 1 is awaiting `LLM-Review`, `Verified`, and unresolved comment checks.","timestamp":1787375757284030001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence for merged commit ed9beb1cba7401ea6fed6b9fd2dd1967f9d6358f\n\n- Gerrit change 2068 held `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` with zero unresolved comments.\n- GitHub Actions run 32553882938 passed every job in 803 seconds without a retry.\n- Gerrit merged the change through a conflict-free rebase and copied both positive labels to the merged revision.\n- `origin/main` contains the merged commit with the canonical `rebar-ticket` trailer, DCO sign-off, and Gerrit Change-Id.\n- The merged diff changes only `docs/README.md`.\n- The documentation index checker, the one-off 67-page uniqueness check, 35 focused documentation tests, lint, type checking, diff checks, and commit-ticket verification passed.\n- Per operator direction, Markdown-only changes do not require a repeated full local suite. Gerrit Verified supplied the current-patch project gate.\n\nCI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"32553882938\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":803,\"fixes_applied\":[],\"retry_count\":0}","timestamp":1787377576627309001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787336373345939001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a47603a7-ba7d-436a-ba40-318b04ac75e7","relation":"blocks","target_id":"ad2e-5db8-7ad0-4fa4"},{"link_uuid":"ef245610-0b24-41de-8e0b-76be8805e509","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1093-ad29-8a66-4321"}],"description":"## Context\n\ndocs/README.md currently combines audience routing, document summaries, taxonomy policy, troubleshooting, generated-artifact ownership, and historical evidence. F01 moves policy and generated ownership to canonical pages. F06 can then make this file one compact landing page without losing discovery paths.\n\n## Current enforcement and history\n\nTicket mucky-like-elkhound added the docs index and scripts/check_docs_index.py. The checker requires every maintained top-level docs Markdown page to appear as a link target. It does not classify pages by audience and does not detect duplicate directory entries. The current landing page also states that ticket links have six relations and that some ADR numbers are shared. Current ticket-model and ADR index behavior no longer supports those statements.\n\n## Plan\n\nRewrite only docs/README.md. Provide labeled routes for clients, contributors, architecture readers, ADR readers, operators, research readers, and evidence readers. Preserve direct discovery for CLI use, MCP use, project adoption, contribution, and internals. Preserve the three existing troubleshooting rows and their remedies. Add one compact directory that links every maintained top-level docs Markdown page exactly once and classifies it under one route. Link subdirectory indexes where they are the correct entry point. Keep the generated inventory on docs/generated-artifacts.md.\n\nRetain bash-migration.md, 88ab-feature-branch-evidence.md, and dco-rollout-evidence.md at their existing paths and list each exactly once as historical evidence. Remove the outdated six-relation statement and the claim that ADR numbers remain shared.\n\n## Exclusions\n\n- No content edits outside docs/README.md.\n- No file relocation or deletion.\n- No generated catalog on the landing page.\n- No new validation behavior. F07 owns validation after this structure lands.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] docs/README.md provides distinct client, contributor, architecture, ADR, operations, research, and evidence routes.\n- [x] The landing page preserves discoverable paths for CLI use, MCP use, adoption, contribution, and internals.\n- [x] The compact directory links every maintained top-level docs Markdown page exactly once.\n- [x] The three existing troubleshooting rows and their remedies remain present.\n- [x] bash-migration.md, 88ab-feature-branch-evidence.md, and dco-rollout-evidence.md remain at their current paths and each appears once in the directory.\n- [x] The landing page contains no generated-artifact tables, no six-relation claim, and no claim that ADR numbers remain shared.\n- [x] scripts/check_docs_index.py --check, make lint, make typecheck, and the project test gate pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"Replace the mixed landing page with audience routes and one complete compact directory."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","ad2e-5db8-7ad0-4fa4"],["parent","b4ec-b899-bb50-4970"],["relates_to","1093-ad29-8a66-4321"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b4ec-b899-bb50-4970","parent_status_uuid":"db26cbca-07d9-426a-98df-edb1b2185520","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["documentation","navigation"],"ticket_id":"513d-67cd-5329-4220","ticket_type":"story","title":"F06 Rebuild documentation navigation by audience","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f7f3773b-2070-436f-b216-2900a1c0dff9","11ea9b14-a8ba-4094-9cf6-e673780ad511","e26205b0-4e14-4e70-9378-8c1a55d61b46","0b68a4dd-7abd-4f07-a44b-f120e156adae","301bba49-df31-4d6c-bd7d-5a6842b6c2a7","4b9bab0d-6a37-48ea-be15-58097d50c4a8","3c5710b0-cedf-42f2-af38-8aa0b39a174e","ef245610-0b24-41de-8e0b-76be8805e509","aa958033-1d99-409f-b321-e9a09d2ce613","db26cbca-07d9-426a-98df-edb1b2185520","c0fe8800-6449-4c62-9f5f-a9021ff83162"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787384171336765001,"uuid":"bfafd850-336f-4b98-9f22-7c9c9279d25c"}